/-! # Flatness and the closed fiber of the local parameter quotient

Source: Stacks Project, Smoothing Ring Maps, proof of Lemma 07FE, steps 10--11.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v w

namespace Algebra

/-- The reduced local map is flat and its closed fiber is ind-smooth over its residue base.

Source: Stacks Project, Smoothing Ring Maps, proof of Lemma 07FE, steps 10--11.
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-popescu-parameter-quotient-local-flat-fiber-data).

Proof: Write P=k[x_i], p=φ⁻¹(q), e=8c, and π_i=φ(x_i). Each π_i lies in q,
since its image in Λ_q belongs to the maximal ideal and that ideal contracts to q.
Thus p contains the origin ideal (x_i); the origin ideal is maximal with quotient k,
so p=(x_i). The d elements π_i generate the maximal ideal of the d-dimensional
regular local ring Λ_q and hence form a regular sequence. The polynomial-origin
localization P_p is regular of dimension d, generated by the x_i. Its local map to
Λ_q is therefore flat by the flat-over-regular criterion.

Localization commutes with quotient: R₀ is canonically P_p/(x_i^e)P_p, and L₀ is
canonically Λ_q/(π_i^e)Λ_q. These isomorphisms send every element coming from P or Λ
to its usual fraction followed by quotient. Their structure-map square commutes,
since it does so on the original rings and inverses of the elements inverted.
Consequently flat quotient base change gives flatness R₀→L₀; the ULift algebra
equivalence identifies this map with R₀→L.

The maximal ideal I of R₀ is generated by the images of x_i, and R₀/I is canonically
k by evaluation at zero. In L₀ the extended ideal IL₀ is generated by the π_i,
and the parameter-generation hypothesis identifies it with the image of the
maximal ideal of Λ_q. Thus L₀/IL₀ is canonically κ(q). Both residue identifications
send constants in k to their original images, so the induced residue-base map is
the given separable extension κ(q)/k. Apply the separable smooth-subalgebra colimit
theorem to that extension. Regard its subalgebras as R₀/I-algebras via R₀/I≃k;
their universal colimit property holds for algebra maps because their inclusions
commute with the constants. Lift their carriers and index category to max(u,v,w),
and use the ULift quotient equivalence L/IL≃L₀/IL₀ followed by the residue-field
identification to obtain the displayed ind-smooth presentation. For d=0 all
parameter ideals are zero; P=k, and hgen says Λ_q has zero maximal ideal, so the
same identifications and field argument apply. No source-algebra factorization
or Popescu resolution is asserted here. -/
theorem parameter_quotient_local_flat_fiber_data
    {k : Type u} {Λ : Type w}
    [Field k] [CommRing Λ] [Algebra k Λ]
    (d c : ℕ) (hc : 1 ≤ c) (φ : MvPolynomial (Fin d) k →ₐ[k] Λ)
    (q : PrimeSpectrum Λ) [IsNoetherianRing Λ]
    [IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)]
    (hdim : ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal) = (d : WithBot ℕ∞))
    (hgen : Ideal.span (Set.range (fun i : Fin d ↦
      algebraMap Λ (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal) (φ (MvPolynomial.X i)))) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal))
    (hsep : IsSeparableExtension k q.asIdeal.ResidueField) :
    letI := φ.toRingHom.toAlgebra
    let J : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k) :=
      Ideal.span (Set.range (fun i : Fin d ↦ (MvPolynomial.X i ^ c) ^ 8))
    let J_Λ := Ideal.map (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k) Λ) J
    ∀ (q₀ : PrimeSpectrum (Λ ⧸ J_Λ)),
      PrimeSpectrum.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk J_Λ) q₀ = q →
    letI := Localization.AtPrime.algebraOfLiesOver
      (q₀.asIdeal.under (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k ⧸ J)) q₀.asIdeal
    let R₀ := Localization.AtPrime (q₀.asIdeal.under (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k ⧸ J))
    let L₀ := Localization.AtPrime q₀.asIdeal
    let L := ULift.{max u v} L₀
    let I := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R₀
    RingHom.Flat (algebraMap R₀ L) ∧
      CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.ind.{max u v w}
        (fun B : CommAlgCat.{max u v w} (R₀ ⧸ I) ↦ Smooth (R₀ ⧸ I) B)
        (CommAlgCat.of (R₀ ⧸ I) (L ⧸ I.map (algebraMap R₀ L))) := by
  sorry

end Algebra
